== diags.every-class
BYN2002 19:5 unknown type `Missing`
BYN5001 8:17 `upserted` changes `this`; name it `upsert`
  help name the member that changes `this` with the plain verb, and keep `-ed` for the copy or view
BYN5002 10:17 `isReady` reads as state but modifies `this`
  label declared `ref this`
  help remove `ref this` so it only reads, or name the action with a verb
BYN5101 11:17 `total` is a noun on a `ref this` member; name the action
  help rename it with the verb for what it does to `this`
BYN5003 16:5 `tryParse` must return `i64?` or `bool`; it is derived from `parse() fails`
  label returns `i64`
  help change it to return `i64?` or `bool`, or remove `tryParse` and call `try parse()`
BYN5001 28:10 `widgeted` changes `this`; name it `widget`
  help name the member that changes `this` with the plain verb, and keep `-ed` for the copy or view
BYN5014 28:10 `widgeted` is not a known verb, noun or adjective
  help add it to `grammar` in package.byn: `verbs: ["widgeted"]`, `nouns: ["widgeted"]` or `adjectives: ["widgeted"]`
BYN5102 33:17 `ready` is a `bool` state; prefix with `is`, `has` or `can`
  help rename it `isReady`
  fix 33:17-33:22 isReady
BYN5014 34:19 `done` is not a known verb, noun or adjective
  help add it to `grammar` in package.byn: `adjectives: ["done"]`, `verbs: ["done"]` or `nouns: ["done"]`
BYN5009 42:9 `at` is a particle; name the member with a verb or a noun
  help rename the member, for example `tryGet(at:)` instead of `at(…)`
BYN5009 43:9 `toList` spells a conversion with `to`; write `List(probe)`
  help use a view noun, `copy()`, or a `T(x)` conversion
BYN5009 44:9 `toString` spells a conversion with `to`; write `string(probe)`
  help use a view noun, `copy()`, or a `T(x)` conversion
BYN5009 45:9 `asSpan` spells a conversion with `as`; write `span`
  help use a view noun, `copy()`, or a `T(x)` conversion
BYN5014 25:10 `hidden` is not a known verb, noun or adjective
  help add it to `grammar` in package.byn: `adjectives: ["hidden"]`, `verbs: ["hidden"]` or `nouns: ["hidden"]`
BYN5102 36:17 `fresh` is a `bool` state; prefix with `is`, `has` or `can`
  help rename it `isFresh`
